"""The questbook's chapters, in order: what each quest asks and pays. Facts come from docs/guide/ (the player guide).

A quest: key (stable: its id is a hash of it, never rename one that has shipped), title, desc (lines; "" is a blank
line), tasks, rewards, deps (keys in this chapter, or "chapter:key"), and optionally subtitle, icon, optional (doesn't
count toward finishing the chapter) and final (the chapter's big last quest).

Tasks: ("item", id[, count]), ("check", "what to do"), ("advancement", id), ("kill", entity, count),
("observe", block, "what to look at"). Rewards: ("item", id[, count]), ("xp", points), ("unlock", blueprint id): the build
joins the Blueprint Table of the player's village (26.10, /workplace unlock). Emeralds and a little
experience; nothing that skips the game.

A chapter's milestone (M27 to M35) keeps it out until that expansion is switched on; needs lists the mods it needs
(comma-separated, or "-").
"""

E = "minecraft:emerald"


def em(n):
    return ("item", E, n)


